WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.840
Major school districts around the country
are searching for new superintendents.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:14.960
In the process, everyone is looking for an
“innovator”—someone with new and exciting ideas.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:21.220
But along the way, a simple truth is too often
lost: We forget that success in any organization,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:25.120
is mostly a matter of precision, discipline,
and focus.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.360
Exciting ideas are only as good as their execution.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:33.360
Too often in the search for innovation, districts
swing back and forth between new programs,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.250
and don’t do any of them especially well.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.879
Teachers and students get swamped by a tide
of ceaseless, half-serious change.

00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:45.900
Some district is inevitably embracing reform
A and rejecting B as misguided . . . just

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:52.010
as another is latching onto B as shiny
and new, and discarding reform A as old and tired.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:57.390
Here’s a suggestion: Don’t ask who's "innovative"
and don't look for a "change agent."

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.540
There's nothing wrong with any of that, but it's a distraction.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.740
What matters much more than what leaders promise

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.020
to do for kids is how they are going to do it.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.620
What do you think districts should look for in a superintendent?

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.500
Let us know in your comments.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.750
Also, let us know what other topics you’d
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.290
and be sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

